It is the intention of a dedicated small group of Linux Users to form
the Toowoomba Linux Users Group.  The focus of this group is to assist
everyday people install and use Linux as a realistic alternative to
Microsoft Windows.  The group will be community focussed assisting
struggling Charity organisations with their computer needs.
It necessary to announce that this group does not intent to take away
membership from the University of Southern Queensland (USQ) Linux
Users Group - which, due to its demographics, focusses on Advanced
Users.  The focus of the Toowoomba Linux Users Group is for the
Beginner and Intermediate User with little or no previous Linux or
programming knowledge.  During recruitment/advertising drives we will
refer advanced users to the USG Linux Users Group.  It is the
intention of the Toowoomba Linux Users Group to have close
communication ties with the USQ Linux Users Group.
Please post comments or objections to: toowoombalinux@googlegroups.com
-
Thank you
Martin Sheridan

